import_gateway.description:
The JUNG HOME Gateway integration (`junghome`) is set up next to this one. Its entities can be taken over here so their entity IDs, names, areas, labels and recorder history continue with the Bluetooth Mesh integration. Matching is by device name (the name from the JUNG HOME app) and entity type; only entities of this integration that you have not renamed or customised yet are replaced.

**{count} entities will move** (gateway entity → replaces):
{matched}

**Kept as they are** (already customised here; the gateway's stays where it is):
{customised}

**No gateway counterpart** (stay as they are):
{unmatched}

**Gateway entities without a counterpart here** (stay with the gateway entry):
{gateway_only}

Submitting unloads both integrations, moves the entities, copies the area, custom name and labels of each matched gateway device to the corresponding device here, disables the gateway entry and reloads this one. Delete the gateway entry afterwards.

abort.nothing_to_import:
No gateway entity is left to take over. Entities of this integration without a counterpart:
{unmatched}

Gateway entities without a counterpart here:
{gateway_only}

abort.import_successful:
{count} entities were taken over from the JUNG HOME Gateway integration:
{matched}

Kept as they were (already customised here):
{customised}

Without a gateway counterpart:
{unmatched}

Still with the gateway entry:
{gateway_only}

The gateway entry has been disabled; delete it under Settings → Devices & services → JUNG HOME once everything looks right.
